{"lesson": {"id": "al_o2_equilibrage", "title": "Équilibrer Al + O₂ → Al₂O₃", "language": "fr", "learning_goal": "Comprendre pourquoi on change les coefficients devant les formules : ce sont des nombres de particules, pas des indices, et chaque atome doit se retrouver pareil des deux côtés."}, "math_context": {"symbols": {}, "expressions": {}}}
{"slice": {"slice_id": "s_base", "introduces": [{"id": "eq", "type": "math", "content": "\\ce{Al + O2 -> Al2O3}", "parts": [{"id": "al_g", "text": "\\ce{Al}"}, {"id": "o2_g", "text": "\\ce{O2}"}, {"id": "fleche", "text": "\\ce{->}"}, {"id": "al2o3_g", "text": "\\ce{Al2O3}"}]}, {"id": "indice_note", "type": "callout", "content": "Les petits chiffres dans Al₂O₃ collent à l'atome : ils ne changent jamais."}, {"id": "coeff_note", "type": "callout", "content": "Les grands chiffres devant comptent les particules : ce sont eux qu'on ajuste."}], "beats": [{"id": "pose", "say": "Bonne question ! D'abord, mettons l'équation au tableau telle qu'elle est écrite.", "cues": [{"id": "c_equation", "text": "l'équation"}], "do": [{"id": "w_eq", "verb": "write", "target": "eq", "at": "cue:c_equation"}]}, {"id": "deux_types", "say": "Ici, il y a deux sortes de chiffres. Les petits chiffres collés, comme le deux et le trois de Al deux O trois, font partie de la molécule. Les grands chiffres devant, on les ajustera.", "cues": [{"id": "c_petits", "text": "petits chiffres collés"}, {"id": "c_grands", "text": "grands chiffres devant"}], "do": [{"id": "s_indice", "verb": "show", "target": "indice_note", "at": "cue:c_petits"}, {"id": "s_coeff", "verb": "show", "target": "coeff_note", "at": "cue:c_grands"}, {"id": "h_al2o3", "verb": "highlight", "target": "eq", "part": "al2o3_g", "role": "accent", "start": "cue:c_petits", "end": "cue_end:c_grands"}], "pause_after": "normal"}]}}
{"slice": {"slice_id": "s_compter", "introduces": [{"id": "tab", "type": "matrix", "params": {"rows": [["1 atome", "2 atomes"], ["2 atomes", "3 atomes"]], "row_labels": ["Al (aluminium)", "O (oxygène)"], "column_labels": ["À gauche (réactifs)", "À droite (produit)"]}}], "beats": [{"id": "tableau", "say": "Comptons ce qu'on a de chaque côté. À gauche : un atome d'aluminium, deux atomes d'oxygène. À droite, dans Al deux O trois : deux aluminiums et trois oxygènes.", "cues": [{"id": "c_comptons", "text": "Comptons"}, {"id": "c_gauche", "text": "À gauche"}, {"id": "c_droite", "text": "À droite"}], "do": [{"id": "s_tab", "verb": "show", "target": "tab", "at": "cue:c_comptons"}, {"id": "h_gauche", "verb": "highlight", "target": "tab", "part": "c1", "role": "given", "start": "cue:c_gauche", "end": "cue_end:c_gauche"}, {"id": "h_droite", "verb": "highlight", "target": "tab", "part": "c2", "role": "accent", "start": "cue:c_droite", "end": "cue_end:c_droite"}]}, {"id": "desequilibre", "say": "Les deux colonnes ne sont pas égales : une réaction ne peut pas créer ni perdre des atomes. Il faut ajuster.", "cues": [{"id": "c_egales", "text": "pas égales"}, {"id": "c_perdre", "text": "perdre"}], "do": [{"id": "h_lignes", "verb": "highlight", "target": "tab", "part": "r2", "role": "unknown", "start": "cue:c_egales", "end": "cue_end:c_perdre"}], "pause_after": "normal"}]}}
{"slice": {"slice_id": "s_multiplier", "introduces": [{"id": "double", "type": "math", "content": "\\ce{2 Al + O2 -> Al2O3}"}, {"id": "gain", "type": "math", "content": "\\ce{2 Al + 3/2 O2 -> Al2O3}"}, {"id": "pourquoi", "type": "callout", "content": "Un grand chiffre devant multiplie toute la formule."}], "beats": [{"id": "met_un_deux", "say": "Devant l'aluminium, mettons un deux. Ce grand deux veut dire deux atomes d'aluminium, pas un indice : la molécule d'aluminium reste Al.", "cues": [{"id": "c_deux", "text": "un deux"}, {"id": "c_deux_atomes", "text": "deux atomes d'aluminium"}], "do": [{"id": "t_eq", "verb": "transform", "source": "eq", "target": "double", "at": "cue:c_deux"}, {"id": "h_double", "verb": "highlight", "target": "double", "role": "accent", "start": "cue:c_deux_atomes", "end": "cue_end:c_deux_atomes"}]}, {"id": "met_oxygene", "say": "Pour l'oxygène, il faut trois atomes à droite. Un O deux en contient deux : il en manque un, donc on prend un O deux et demi. Un indice trois demis, entre autres, peut être temporaire.", "cues": [{"id": "c_trois", "text": "trois atomes"}, {"id": "c_demi", "text": "un O deux et demi"}], "do": [{"id": "t_gain", "verb": "transform", "source": "double", "target": "gain", "at": "cue:c_trois"}, {"id": "h_gain", "verb": "highlight", "target": "gain", "role": "accent", "start": "cue:c_demi", "end": "cue_end:c_demi"}, {"id": "s_pourquoi", "verb": "show", "target": "pourquoi", "at": "after:t_gain"}], "pause_after": "normal"}]}}
{"slice": {"slice_id": "s_entiers", "introduces": [{"id": "propre", "type": "math", "content": "\\ce{4 Al + 3 O2 -> 2 Al2O3}", "parts": [{"id": "quatre_al", "text": "\\ce{4 Al}"}, {"id": "trois_o2", "text": "\\ce{3 O2}"}, {"id": "fleche2", "text": "\\ce{->}"}, {"id": "deux_al2o3", "text": "\\ce{2 Al2O3}"}]}, {"id": "verif", "type": "matrix", "params": {"rows": [["4 atomes", "4 atomes"], ["6 atomes", "6 atomes"]], "row_labels": ["Al (aluminium)", "O (oxygène)"], "column_labels": ["À gauche", "À droite"]}}], "beats": [{"id": "doubler", "say": "Pour éviter les fractions, on multiplie toute l'équation par deux : quatre Al, trois O deux, et deux Al deux O trois.", "cues": [{"id": "c_par_deux", "text": "par deux"}, {"id": "c_quatre", "text": "quatre Al"}], "do": [{"id": "f_notes", "verb": "fade_out", "target": "indice_note", "at": "cue:c_par_deux"}, {"id": "f_coeff", "verb": "fade_out", "target": "coeff_note", "at": "cue:c_par_deux"}, {"id": "t_propre", "verb": "transform", "source": "gain", "target": "propre", "at": "cue:c_par_deux"}, {"id": "h_quatre", "verb": "highlight", "target": "propre", "part": "quatre_al", "role": "result", "start": "cue:c_quatre", "end": "cue_end:c_quatre"}]}, {"id": "verifier", "say": "Vérifions : à gauche quatre aluminiums et six oxygènes ; à droite deux Al deux O trois donnent aussi quatre aluminiums et six oxygènes. Les deux colonnes sont égales, l'équation est équilibrée.", "cues": [{"id": "c_verifions", "text": "Vérifions"}, {"id": "c_egales_fin", "text": "colonnes sont égales"}, {"id": "c_equilibree", "text": "équilibrée"}], "do": [{"id": "s_verif", "verb": "show", "target": "verif", "at": "cue:c_verifions"}, {"id": "h_verif", "verb": "highlight", "target": "verif", "role": "result", "start": "cue:c_egales_fin", "end": "cue_end:c_equilibree"}], "pause_after": "normal"}]}}
{"slice": {"slice_id": "s_retenir", "introduces": [{"id": "regle", "type": "math", "content": "\\ce{4 Al + 3 O2 -> 2 Al2O3}", "style": {"role": "result"}}, {"id": "idee", "type": "text", "content": "Les indices sont figés ; on ajuste les coefficients devant jusqu'à avoir le même nombre d'atomes de chaque côté."}], "beats": [{"id": "retenir", "say": "À retenir : les petits indices font partie des molécules et ne bougent pas. On change les grands chiffres devant, parce qu'ils comptent les particules, jusqu'à ce que chaque atome se retrouve en même nombre des deux côtés.", "cues": [{"id": "c_retenir", "text": "À retenir"}, {"id": "c_change", "text": "change les grands chiffres devant"}], "do": [{"id": "f_rest", "verb": "fade_out", "target": "tab", "at": "cue:c_retenir"}, {"id": "f_verif", "verb": "fade_out", "target": "verif", "at": "cue:c_retenir"}, {"id": "f_pourquoi", "verb": "fade_out", "target": "pourquoi", "at": "cue:c_retenir"}, {"id": "cadre", "verb": "camera.focus", "targets": ["regle", "idee"], "bounds": "layout_bounds", "at": "cue:c_retenir"}, {"id": "s_idee", "verb": "show", "target": "idee", "at": "cue:c_change"}, {"id": "h_coeff_fin", "verb": "highlight", "target": "propre", "part": "trois_o2", "role": "accent", "start": "cue:c_change", "end": "cue_end:c_change"}]}]}}
